    "text": "To determine how many donuts Gamma received, we start by defining the number of donuts Gamma received as \\( G \\). According to the problem, Beta took three times as many donuts as Gamma, so Beta received \\( 3G \\) donuts. Delta took 8 donuts. The total number of donuts is 40, so we can write the equation:\n\n\\[ 8 + 3G + G = 40 \\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[ 8 + 4G = 40 \\]\n\nNext, we isolate \\( G \\) by subtracting 8 from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 4G = 32 \\]\n\nThen, we solve for \\( G \\) by dividing both sides by 4:\n\n\\[ G = 8 \\]\n\nSo, Gamma received \\(\\boxed{8}\\) donuts.",
